  "consumers": {
    "description": "What every consumer of the bone frames must show of the left clavicle (0.17 m, profile ±0.02 m along its normal v and ±0.015 m along its joint axis w, origin [0, 1.48, 0.02]). Lifted by θ about its own joint axis its axis is u = [0, sin θ, cos θ] and its normal v = [0, cos θ, -sin θ], so its corners are at height 1.48 + L·sin θ ± 0.02·cos θ and at 0.02 + L·cos θ ∓ 0.02·sin θ beside the plane (L = 0 or 0.17) and ±0.015 ahead: the boxes below for θ = 30° (pose shrug, clip key at 0.5 s) and θ = 15° (the clip at 0.25 s, linear ease), as [min, max] per drawing axis in metres. The capsule (radius 0.015 m on the bone axis) spans the axis ends ± its radius. The arm (3.75 kg, centre of mass 0.27 m down the arm) hangs from the clavicle tip 0.17 m beside the sternoclavicular joint: the joint carries 3.75 · 9.80665 = 36.7749375 N of shear along the clavicle normal and 36.7749375 · 0.17 = 6.251739375 N·m of bending about the clavicle's joint axis, falling linearly to zero at the tip. The figure holds its breath in these cases (the respiration moves no bone), so the clip instants are the pure interpolation of the keys. The bending acts in the frontal plane (moment vector along ahead), so its diagram is drawn over the baseline from (0.02, 1.48) to (0.19, 1.48) in the front elevation, has no ordinate in the side elevation (which looks along the bone) and is an out-of-plane mark in the plan (which looks along the ordinate).",
